        "thinking": "I'm identifying जुघुटिध्वे as लिट् मध्यम बहुवचन आत्मनेपद of घुट् (घुट परिवर्तने, भ्वादि, द्युतादि group, आत्मनेपदी, सेट्), noting that द्युतादि verbs take परस्मैपद optionally in लुङ्. Now I'm moving on to consider the आशीर्लिङ् आत्मनेपद forms.\n\nFor आशीर्लिङ् मध्यम बहुवचन, I'm working out that घोटिषीध्वम् can optionally become घोटिषीढ्वम् via विभाषेटः (8.3.79), since इणः षीध्वंलुङ्लिटां धोऽङ्गात् (8.3.78) ordinarily mandates ढ when इण् directly precedes षीध्वम्, but here इट् intervenes, making the ढ change optional rather than compulsory. I'm also checking whether guna applies, reasoning that since this is सेट् (इट् intervenes), the कित् condition from लिङ्सिचावात्मनेपदेषु (1.2.11) — which requires a झल्-initial ending without इट् — doesn't apply here, so the form isn't treated as कित् for this purpose.\n\nI'm also double-checking that घुट् here belongs to भ्वादिगण (meaning परिवर्तन, \"to change/turn\"), distinguishing it from the कुटादि root घुट् \"to obstruct\" (गण्कुटादिभ्योऽञ्णिद्ङित्) which is परस्मैपदी and thus irrelevant since जुघुटिध्वे is आत्मनेपद. So the final answer settles on घोटिषीध्वम्.\n\n",
